 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "hero-01",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Pronouns that hold on.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-02",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Some pronouns are written joined to the end of another word.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "sub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-03",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "His book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-04",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُهُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-05",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "On it.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-06",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "عَلَيْهِ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَيْهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-07",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "He opened it.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-08",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فَتَحَهُ",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:فَتَحَهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-title-01",
   "scene": "c01-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter one. The twelve attached pronouns.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-intro-01",
   "scene": "c01-intro",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "An attached pronoun cannot stand alone.",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "b:0",
    "hl:cannot stand alone"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-intro-02",
   "scene": "c01-intro",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It joins the end of a noun, a preposition or a verb.",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "hl:a noun, a preposition or a verb"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-intro-03",
   "scene": "c01-intro",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Like the separate pronouns, it is fixed.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "hl:it is fixed"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-01",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Here are all twelve. Each row shows the pronoun, who it means, the pronoun on a noun, and the English.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "b:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-02",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for I, or me. My book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:0",
    "ar:ـي"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-03",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابِي",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابِي"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-04",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for we, or us. Our book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:1",
    "ar:ـنَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-05",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُنَا",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُنَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-06",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for you, one man. Your book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:2",
    "ar:ـكَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-07",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُكَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُكَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-08",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for you, one woman. Your book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:3",
    "ar:ـكِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-09",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُكِ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُكِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-10",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for you, two. Your book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:4",
    "ar:ـكُمَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-11",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُكُمَا",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُكُمَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-12",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for you, men, or a mixed group. Your book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:5",
    "ar:ـكُمْ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-13",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُكُمْ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُكُمْ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-14",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for you, women. Your book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:6",
    "ar:ـكُنَّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-15",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُكُنَّ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُكُنَّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-16",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for he, or it. His book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:7",
    "ar:ـهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-17",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُهُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-18",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for she, or it. Her book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:8",
    "ar:ـهَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-19",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُهَا",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُهَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-20",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for they, two. Their book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:9",
    "ar:ـهُمَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-21",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُهُمَا",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُهُمَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-22",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for they, men, or a mixed group. Their book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:10",
    "ar:ـهُمْ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-23",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُهُمْ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُهُمْ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-24",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for they, women. Their book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:11",
    "ar:ـهُنَّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-25",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُهُنَّ",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُهُنَّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-tip-01",
   "scene": "c01-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Tip. Compare them with the separate pronouns of unit one.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "b:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-tip-02",
   "scene": "c01-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "أَنْتُمَا",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:أَنْتُمَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-tip-03",
   "scene": "c01-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "and the attached pronoun for you, two.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـكُمَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-tip-04",
   "scene": "c01-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "أَنْتُمْ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:أَنْتُمْ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-tip-05",
   "scene": "c01-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "and the attached pronoun for you, men or a mixed group.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـكُمْ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-tip-06",
   "scene": "c01-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "أَنْتُنَّ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:أَنْتُنَّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-tip-07",
   "scene": "c01-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "and the attached pronoun for you, women.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـكُنَّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-tip-08",
   "scene": "c01-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The family of this pronoun means you.",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـكَ",
    "hl:family is \"you\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-tip-09",
   "scene": "c01-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The family of this one means he, she and they.",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـهُ",
    "hl:family is \"he, she, they\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-title-01",
   "scene": "c02-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter two. On a noun: the owner.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-owner-01",
   "scene": "c02-owner",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A pronoun on a noun shows who owns it.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "b:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-owner-02",
   "scene": "c02-owner",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It works like the second word of an iḍāfa.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-owner-03",
   "scene": "c02-owner",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Zayd's book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "b:1",
    "ex:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-owner-04",
   "scene": "c02-owner",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُ زَيْدٍ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُ زَيْدٍ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-owner-05",
   "scene": "c02-owner",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "His book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-owner-06",
   "scene": "c02-owner",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُهُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-owner-07",
   "scene": "c02-owner",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Zayd is the owner, so it is jarr.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "note:0",
    "ar:زَيْدٍ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-owner-08",
   "scene": "c02-owner",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for he takes its job.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-owner-09",
   "scene": "c02-owner",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "His book is new.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-owner-10",
   "scene": "c02-owner",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُهُ جَدِيدٌ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُهُ جَدِيدٌ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-owner-11",
   "scene": "c02-owner",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for he is the owner.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "note:1",
    "ar:ـهُ#2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-owner-12",
   "scene": "c02-owner",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It is fixed, so it does not change its ending. It is in the place of jarr.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-owner-13",
   "scene": "c02-owner",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فِي مَحَلِّ جَرٍّ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:فِي مَحَلِّ جَرٍّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-owner-14",
   "scene": "c02-owner",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Her house is near.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-owner-15",
   "scene": "c02-owner",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "بَيْتُهَا قَرِيبٌ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:بَيْتُهَا قَرِيبٌ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-owner-16",
   "scene": "c02-owner",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for she is the owner, in the place of jarr.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "note:2",
    "ar:ـهَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-rule-01",
   "scene": "c02-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "No al, no tanween.",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "b:0",
    "ar:ال",
    "hl:no tanween"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-rule-02",
   "scene": "c02-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A noun with an attached pronoun is the first word of an iḍāfa.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "hl:the first word of an iḍāfa"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-rule-03",
   "scene": "c02-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "So it has no al and no tanween.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ال#2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-rule-04",
   "scene": "c02-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A book,",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-rule-05",
   "scene": "c02-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابٌ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابٌ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-rule-06",
   "scene": "c02-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "becomes his book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-rule-07",
   "scene": "c02-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُهُ",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-endings-01",
   "scene": "c02-endings",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The noun still shows its own ending before the pronoun.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "b:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-endings-02",
   "scene": "c02-endings",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Only the noun is flexible. The pronoun stays the same.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-endings-03",
   "scene": "c02-endings",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "His book is new.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "b:1",
    "ex:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-endings-04",
   "scene": "c02-endings",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُهُ جَدِيدٌ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُهُ جَدِيدٌ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-endings-05",
   "scene": "c02-endings",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The word for book is the Topic. It is rafʿ, with damma.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:0",
    "ar:كِتَابُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-endings-06",
   "scene": "c02-endings",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-endings-07",
   "scene": "c02-endings",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The student read his book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-endings-08",
   "scene": "c02-endings",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "قَرَأَ الطَّالِبُ كِتَابَهُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:قَرَأَ الطَّالِبُ كِتَابَهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-endings-09",
   "scene": "c02-endings",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The word for book is the object. It is naṣb, with fatha.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:1",
    "ar:كِتَابَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-endings-10",
   "scene": "c02-endings",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-endings-11",
   "scene": "c02-endings",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pen is in his book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-endings-12",
   "scene": "c02-endings",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "القَلَمُ فِي كِتَابِهِ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:القَلَمُ فِي كِتَابِهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-endings-13",
   "scene": "c02-endings",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The word for book comes after the preposition meaning in. It is jarr, with kasra.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:2",
    "ar:كِتَابِ",
    "ar:فِي"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-endings-14",
   "scene": "c02-endings",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابِ",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-01",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A spelling tip. Look at a word that ends in this letter.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "b:0",
    "ar:ة"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-02",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Before a pronoun, it is written as this letter instead.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ت"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-03",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A car.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-04",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "سَيَّارَةٌ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:سَيَّارَةٌ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-05",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "His car.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-06",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "سَيَّارَتُهُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:سَيَّارَتُهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-07",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A room.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-08",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "غُرْفَةٌ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:غُرْفَةٌ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-09",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Her room.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-10",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "غُرْفَتُهَا",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:غُرْفَتُهَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-title-01",
   "scene": "c03-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter three.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-title-02",
   "scene": "c03-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "With the pronoun for me, the ending is hidden.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـي"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-hidden-01",
   "scene": "c03-hidden",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for me always needs a kasra before it.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "b:0",
    "ar:ـي#2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-hidden-02",
   "scene": "c03-hidden",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "So the noun cannot show damma, fatha or kasra of its own.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-hidden-03",
   "scene": "c03-hidden",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "My book is new.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "b:1",
    "ex:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-hidden-04",
   "scene": "c03-hidden",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابِي جَدِيدٌ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابِي جَدِيدٌ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-hidden-05",
   "scene": "c03-hidden",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The word for book is the Topic, and it is rafʿ. But you see a kasra.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "note:0",
    "ar:كِتَابِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-hidden-06",
   "scene": "c03-hidden",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pen is in my book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-hidden-07",
   "scene": "c03-hidden",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "القَلَمُ فِي كِتَابِي",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:القَلَمُ فِي كِتَابِي"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-hidden-08",
   "scene": "c03-hidden",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Here the word for book is jarr. It looks the same.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "note:1",
    "ar:كِتَابِ#2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-rule-01",
   "scene": "c03-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "So here is the rule. Do not read the ending before the pronoun for me.",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "b:0",
    "ar:ـي#2",
    "hl:Do not read the ending before"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-rule-02",
   "scene": "c03-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Before it, the kasra is for the pronoun.",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـي#3",
    "hl:the kasra is for the pronoun"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-rule-03",
   "scene": "c03-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Find the job of the noun from the sentence, never from this vowel.",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "hl:from the sentence, never from this vowel"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-title-01",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter four. On a preposition.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-01",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A pronoun after a preposition is jarr, like any word after a preposition.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "b:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-02",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It is fixed, so it is in the place of jarr.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-03",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pen is yours. That is, for you.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "b:1",
    "ex:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-04",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "القَلَمُ لَكَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:القَلَمُ لَكَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-05",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for you, one man, comes after the preposition meaning for.",
   "pause": 0.2,
   "cues": [
    "note:0",
    "ar:ـكَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-06",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "That preposition is only one letter.",
   "pause": 0.2,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-07",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun is in the place of jarr.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-08",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "He went out of it.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-09",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "خَرَجَ مِنْهُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:خَرَجَ مِنْهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-10",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for it comes after the preposition meaning from.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:1",
    "ar:ـهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-11",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مِنْ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:مِنْ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-12",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It is in the place of jarr too.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-13",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The book is on it.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-14",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الكِتَابُ عَلَيْهِ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:الكِتَابُ عَلَيْهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-15",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Here the pronoun for it comes after the preposition meaning on.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:2",
    "ar:ـهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-16",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "عَلَى",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَى"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-17",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It is in the place of jarr. Its kasra is not a sign of jarr. Only the sound changes. Chapter five explains it.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-01",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Some prepositions change their shape. Learn these forms.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "b:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-02",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Each row has the preposition, then the preposition with the pronoun for he, for you, and for me.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "b:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-03",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "In. In it, in you, in me.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-04",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فِي",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:فِي"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-05",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فِيهِ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:فِيهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-06",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فِيكَ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:فِيكَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-07",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فِيَّ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:فِيَّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-08",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "On. On it, on you, on me.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-09",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "عَلَى",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَى"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-10",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "عَلَيْهِ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَيْهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-11",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "عَلَيْكَ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَيْكَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-12",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "عَلَيَّ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَيَّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-13",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "To. To it, to you, to me.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-14",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "إِلَى",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:إِلَى"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-15",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "إِلَيْهِ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:إِلَيْهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-16",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "إِلَيْكَ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:إِلَيْكَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-17",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "إِلَيَّ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:إِلَيَّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-18",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "From. From it, from you, from me.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-19",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مِنْ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:مِنْ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-20",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مِنْهُ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:مِنْهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-21",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مِنْكَ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:مِنْكَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-22",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مِنِّي",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:مِنِّي"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-23",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "For. This one is a single letter. For him, for you, for me.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:4",
    "ar:لِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-24",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "لَهُ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لَهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-25",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "لَكَ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لَكَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-26",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "لِي",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لِي"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-01",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Three changes to remember.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "b:0",
    "hl:Three changes to remember"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-02",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "One. The preposition meaning on.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-03",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "عَلَى",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَى"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-04",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Before a pronoun, its end changes to this shape.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَيْـ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-05",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "On it.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-06",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "عَلَيْهِ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَيْهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-07",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Two. The preposition meaning to.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-08",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "إِلَى",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:إِلَى"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-09",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Its end changes in the same way.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "ar:إِلَيْـ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-10",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "To her.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-11",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "إِلَيْهَا",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:إِلَيْهَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-12",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Three. The preposition meaning for is one letter with a kasra.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-13",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Before a pronoun, it takes a fatha.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-14",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "For him, for you, for her.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-15",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "لَهُ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لَهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-16",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "لَكَ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لَكَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-17",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "لَهَا",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لَهَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-18",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Only with the pronoun for me does it keep its kasra. For me.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـي",
    "hl:it stays"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-19",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "لِي",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لِي"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-title-01",
   "scene": "c05-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter five. When the pronoun for he",
   "pause": 0.15,
   "cues": [
    "title",
    "ar:ـهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-title-02",
   "scene": "c05-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "changes its damma to a kasra.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-rule-01",
   "scene": "c05-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "After a kasra, or after this letter,",
   "pause": 0.2,
   "cues": [
    "b:0",
    "ar:ي#2",
    "hl:After kasra or"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-rule-02",
   "scene": "c05-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "the damma of the pronoun for he becomes a kasra.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـهُ#2",
    "hl:becomes a kasra"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-rule-03",
   "scene": "c05-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "After this letter: in it, on it, to him.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-rule-04",
   "scene": "c05-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فِيهِ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:فِيهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-rule-05",
   "scene": "c05-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "عَلَيْهِ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَيْهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-rule-06",
   "scene": "c05-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "إِلَيْهِ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:إِلَيْهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-rule-07",
   "scene": "c05-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "After a kasra: with it, and in his house.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-rule-08",
   "scene": "c05-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "بِهِ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:بِهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-rule-09",
   "scene": "c05-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فِي بَيْتِهِ",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:فِي بَيْتِهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-01",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The same happens to three more pronouns.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "b:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-02",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "They, two.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـهُمَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-03",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "They, men.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـهُمْ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-04",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "And they, women.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـهُنَّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-05",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "On them.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "b:1",
    "ex:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-06",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "عَلَيْهِمْ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَيْهِمْ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-07",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for they, men,",
   "pause": 0.15,
   "cues": [
    "note:0",
    "ar:ـهُمْ#2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-08",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "comes after this letter,",
   "pause": 0.15,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ي"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-09",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "so its damma becomes a kasra.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـهِمْ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-10",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "In them, two.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-11",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فِيهِمَا",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:فِيهِمَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-12",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for they, two,",
   "pause": 0.15,
   "cues": [
    "note:1",
    "ar:ـهُمَا#2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-13",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "comes after the same letter,",
   "pause": 0.15,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ي#2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-14",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "so it changes in the same way.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـهِمَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-15",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "In their house, women.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-16",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فِي بَيْتِهِنَّ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:فِي بَيْتِهِنَّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-17",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The word for house ends in a kasra here. It is jarr after the preposition meaning in.",
   "pause": 0.2,
   "cues": [
    "note:2",
    "ar:بَيْتِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-18",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for they, women, comes after it,",
   "pause": 0.15,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـهُنَّ#2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-19",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "so its damma becomes a kasra too.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـهِنَّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-01",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Tip. It is the same pronoun.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "b:0",
    "hl:It is the same pronoun"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-02",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Only the sound changes, to make it easy to say.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "hl:Only the sound changes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-03",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "With a damma, a fatha or a sukūn before it, it stays as it is.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـهُ#2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-04",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "After a sukūn: from him.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-05",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مِنْهُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:مِنْهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-06",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "After a fatha: for him.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-07",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "لَهُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لَهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-08",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "After a damma: his book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-09",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُهُ",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كِتَابُهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-title-01",
   "scene": "c06-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter six. On a verb: the object.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-intro-01",
   "scene": "c06-intro",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Put one of the twelve pronouns on a past verb or an order verb, and it is the object.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "b:0",
    "hl:is the object"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-intro-02",
   "scene": "c06-intro",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The object is naṣb.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "hl:The object is naṣb"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-intro-03",
   "scene": "c06-intro",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun is fixed, so it is in the place of naṣb.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "hl:in the place of naṣb"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-intro-04",
   "scene": "c06-intro",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فِي مَحَلِّ نَصْبٍ",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:فِي مَحَلِّ نَصْبٍ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-01",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "He opened the door.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "b:0",
    "ex:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-02",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فَتَحَ البَابَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:فَتَحَ البَابَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-03",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "He opened it.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-04",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فَتَحَهُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:فَتَحَهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-05",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for it takes the place of the door.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:0",
    "ar:ـهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-06",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "البَابَ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:البَابَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-07",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The girl opened it.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-08",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فَتَحَتْهُ البِنْتُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:فَتَحَتْهُ البِنْتُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-09",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun comes right after the verb, before the doer.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "note:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-10",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The teacher wrote it. It means the letter.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-11",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبَهَا المُدَرِّسُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:كَتَبَهَا المُدَرِّسُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-12",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "In Arabic, the word for a letter you write is feminine. So we use the pronoun for she.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "note:2",
    "ar:ـهَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-13",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It is the object, in the place of naṣb.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-14",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Read the book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-15",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "اِقْرَأِ الكِتَابَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:اِقْرَأِ الكِتَابَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-16",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Read it.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-17",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "اِقْرَأْهُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:اِقْرَأْهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-18",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Before al, the order verb had a small helping kasra, only to make it easy to say. It is not jarr.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "note:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-19",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "With the pronoun, the order verb keeps its sukūn.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:اِقْرَأْ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-20",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "اِقْرَأْ",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "ar:اِقْرَأْ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-21",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Then the pronoun for it is added.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـهُ#2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-22",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Write it.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-23",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "اُكْتُبْهُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:اُكْتُبْهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-ex-24",
   "scene": "c06-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for it is the object, in the place of naṣb.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "note:4",
    "ar:ـهُ#3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-tips-01",
   "scene": "c06-tips",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Tip. Past verbs also have endings for the doer.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "b:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-tips-02",
   "scene": "c06-tips",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "I,",
   "pause": 0.2,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـتُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-tips-03",
   "scene": "c06-tips",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "you,",
   "pause": 0.2,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـتَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-tips-04",
   "scene": "c06-tips",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "and we.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـنَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-tips-05",
   "scene": "c06-tips",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "They are pronouns too. We learn them in unit six.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "hl:They are pronouns too"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-tips-06",
   "scene": "c06-tips",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "One more tip. On a verb, the pronoun for me has an extra letter.",
   "pause": 0.2,
   "cues": [
    "b:1",
    "ar:ـنِي"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-tips-07",
   "scene": "c06-tips",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "This one.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ن"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-tips-08",
   "scene": "c06-tips",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "We meet it later.",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "hl:We meet it later"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c07-title-01",
   "scene": "c07-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter seven. Three places, one table.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c07-table-01",
   "scene": "c07-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Here is the whole lesson in one table. What is the pronoun joined to? What is its job? What place is it in?",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "b:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c07-table-02",
   "scene": "c07-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Joined to a noun, it is the owner, in the place of jarr. His book.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c07-table-03",
   "scene": "c07-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابُهُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
